# p_e5f6 — Marco runs before work on weekdays

Marco is an early riser who goes for a 45-minute run from 6:30 to 7:15 on weekdays before settling at his desk. He takes his running shoes, water bottle, and jacket with him. Omar stays in until about 7:00 and does his morning routine. After the run, Marco showers, changes, and is at his desk by 9:00. The rest of the week follows a standard dual-WFH pattern. What sets this hypothesis apart: running_shoes_marco, water_bottle_marco, and jacket_marco are OUT_OF_HOUSE between 6:30 and 7:15 on weekdays. The 03:00 patrol will still find them at the shoe rack and dish rack because the run hasn't happened yet. What would refute it: running_shoes_marco sighted at shoe_rack_e1 at 06:45 on a weekday, or water_bottle_marco at dish_rack_k1 at that time.

